# Publish to GitHub Pages by default

When the user asks for website changes (content, assets, Practice app, quiz, styles, build scripts), treat **deploying to GitHub Pages** as part of finishing the work unless they explicitly say not to publish.

## After changes that affect the live site

1. Keep sources of truth under `content/`, `assets/`, `templates/`, `scripts/` — do not hand-edit `output/`.
2. Run `py scripts/build_site.py` (and `py scripts/build_curriculum.py` when curriculum JSON changes).
3. Commit the relevant source changes (not secrets).
4. Push to `main` so `.github/workflows/deploy-pages.yml` deploys.
5. Confirm the workflow succeeds when practical.
6. Report the live URLs:
   - https://tehghost99.github.io/yt2site/
   - https://tehghost99.github.io/yt2site/practice.html

## Do not publish when

- The user says not to publish, deploy, push, or commit
- Changes are local-only experiments they asked to keep uncommitted
- Files contain secrets (API keys, `.env`, credentials)

## Notes

- GitHub Pages builds from the repo via Actions; pushing `main` is the deploy.
- Appwrite web platforms must include `tehghost99.github.io` for auth/sync on the live site.
